  "body": "**Apply the quality-binding correction in #2984 before machine use or merge.** The control resolved generic work quality names to different resident targets in this test.\n\nStacked on #2981. Review the [larger punch group changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/f53d50d77c7b06ed2407cedfa9c16627f8655f43...c81cfd1d44c0c210d5ba8ddc0fb1a63c3ac81342).\n\nUse two to nine punches with one-digit resource suffixes. Each captured punch must have its own complete solid in the setup. Account for every model and every operation. Check the compensated cutting and threading envelopes for every pair of works, including pairs that are apart in the operation list. An unsafe overlap stops the entire export.\n\nEach work gets its own geometry file, resource, threading hole, captured separation and resident quality object. The job directory is published only after the complete set is ready. The saved single-work and two-work examples keep their original output.\n\nRun the three-work example with `cargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/punch-trio.camscript`. Run the nine-work case with `cargo run -p camcraft-app --bin camcraft-cli -- script examples/agie/punch-grid.camscript`.\n\nAgie Control resolved all nine distinct resources and threading positions in the direct nine-work job. It ran 72 cutting blocks. All 144 face and offset measurements passed. The 36 distinct pairs had disjoint cutting envelopes, and each rough separation measured 1.000 mm. The three-work case gave 24 cutting blocks. Both formal checks reported zero job errors and the expected manual setup and option 131072 warnings. No physical cut was made. The first and ninth generic quality names in the nine-work case selected different resident finish targets.\n\nThe independent gate passed 31 app tests, 18 native post tests and strict Clippy for app, geometry and post. The integrated branch exported 20 jobs and preserved all 72 files on repeat export.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The native Agie post accepts larger groups of independent captured punches. It checks source ownership and clearance for every pair before publishing the job.\n\nFixes #2980\n",
